cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Transept core, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Transept core: multiobjective, structure-guided multiple sequence alignment of transmembrane proteins"
version: "0.9"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/jMetal/Transept-core"
abstract: >-
  Transept core refines multiple sequence alignments of transmembrane proteins with multiobjective
  evolutionary algorithms. It optimises a topology-aware sum of pairs and a structural consistency
  score computed from AlphaFold2 models, never splits a transmembrane helix, and returns a set of
  trade-off alignments. It is the engine of the Transept interface.
keywords:
  - multiple sequence alignment
  - transmembrane proteins
  - G protein-coupled receptors
  - multiobjective optimisation
  - AlphaFold2
  - jMetal
